From: enfs-dkms
Subject: [PATCH] include/linux/nfs_xdr.h: add struct nfs_extend_xdr_arg

enfs's NFSv3 extended-call support (fs/nfs/enfs/exten_call.c) needs a
small carrier struct for the extra XDR payload appended to certain v3
operations. The struct is consumed by both nfs.ko (after our fs/nfs/
nfs3xdr.c patch encodes/decodes it) and by enfs.ko itself.

We append it after the nfs_rpc_ops vtable struct (the last data struct
in the file before the helper-function block), guarded by CONFIG_ENFS.

NOTE: this struct enables a non-standard extension to the NFSv3 wire
format. Standard NFSv3 servers that don't speak the OpenEuler extension
will reject calls that carry it. Documented as a compat risk in
docs/PORTING-NOTES.md § "nfs3xdr v3 wire format".

---
 include/linux/nfs_xdr.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/include/linux/nfs_xdr.h
+++ b/include/linux/nfs_xdr.h
@@ -1858,6 +1858,14 @@ struct nfs_rpc_ops {
 	void	(*enable_swap)(struct inode *inode);
 	void	(*disable_swap)(struct inode *inode);
 };
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ENFS)
+struct nfs_extend_xdr_arg {
+	int	 maxsize;
+	int	 buflen;
+	char	*pBuf;
+};
+#endif

 /*
  * Helper functions used by NFS client and/or server
